<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 4.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!-- Slurs whose end isn't attached to a note: a slur start and a slur stop with the same number on the same note,
  as Dolet for Sibelius writes e.g. a slur running into a repeat barline (see PR #1516). Drawn from a measure's last note
  to the barline, and not at all from an earlier note.
  m.1: last note, stem up -> drawn below, to the barline.
  m.2: last note, stem down, backward repeat -> drawn above, ends before the repeat sign. Same slur number as m.1 right
       after it: its own stop doesn't end the slur of m.1.
  m.3: first note (mid-measure) -> not drawn.
  m.4: last note, but a later stop of its number in m.5 ends it -> a normal slur to m.5.
  m.5: last note, stop written before the start (and nothing open to end) -> drawn to the final barline. -->
